## Context

Child of tickets/1004, blocked by 1005 (records must exist to backfill).
The `defects-confirmed-post-merge` line (spec §4, §5.3) is the only source
of the pair table's "neither" cell and the only thing that makes a game
defect-bearing; without it, correlation estimates skew optimistic and
the labeled corpus stays empty (the audition board's structural zero).

## Actions

1. Extend roar step 3's sweep ("review the fix just completed — grep for
   the same anti-pattern") with one hook: when the fix touches lines a
   past PR's review covered, backfill `defects-confirmed-post-merge` in
   that PR's attribution record with basename:line anchors.
2. Backfill is append-only and factual; roar never re-judges the original
   review.
3. Tests: a simulated post-merge fix updates the referenced record and
   nothing else; a fix with no covered past review is a no-op.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A post-merge fix backfills the original PR's attribution record
- [ ] Backfilled records are visible to the 1007 read surfaces as
      defect-bearing games
